{%- comment -%}
  eBook consent (§ 17(10) and § 19(1)(m) zákona 108/2024 Z. z.).
  Shown when the cart contains an item that needs no shipping (= digital: eBook via Digital Products).
  The checkbox is required and belongs to the cart form, so the browser blocks "Check out" until it is ticked.

  UX: the consent is one sentence with the box, not a wall of text. The legal
  declaration is complete and unchanged — it is the sentence the law asks for —
  but the explanation behind it moved into a disclosure, so the last screen
  before payment reads as a confirmation rather than an obstacle. Shopify Basic
  cannot put this in the checkout: checkout extensibility is Plus-only, so the
  cart is the last place we control. See docs/legal/ebook-consent.md.
  The declaration is saved as a cart attribute and appears on the order ("eBook consent").
  Accepts:
  - form_id: {String} id of the cart <form> ('cart' on the cart page, 'CartDrawer-Form' in the drawer)
  Note: relies on digital variants having "requires shipping" off and printed ones on (see LAUNCH-READINESS D2).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign has_ebook = false
  for item in cart.items
    if item.requires_shipping == false
      assign has_ebook = true
      break
    endif
  endfor
-%}
{%- if has_ebook -%}
  <div class="wui-consent" data-ebook-consent>
    <label class="wui-check wui-consent__label" for="EbookConsent-{{ form_id }}">
      <input
        type="checkbox"
        id="EbookConsent-{{ form_id }}"
        class="wui-check__box"
        name="attributes[eBook consent]"
        value="{{ 'walterin.ebook_consent.declaration' | t | escape }}"
        form="{{ form_id }}"
        required
      >
      <span class="wui-check__text">{{ 'walterin.ebook_consent.declaration' | t }}</span>
    </label>
    <details class="wui-consent__more">
      <summary>{{ 'walterin.ebook_consent.more' | t }}</summary>
      <p>{{ 'walterin.ebook_consent.notice' | t }}</p>
    </details>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
